    "body": "Closes #82\n\nAdds selection-based molecular minimization with an explicit, fixed physical context.\nThe lightning button beside Edit opens setup; Ctrl+M immediately captures and starts\nan isolated calculation with up to 500 iterations. Reports and nonpickable previews precede an\nexplicit Apply, which updates selected coordinates in one exact multi-entry Undo/Redo\ncommand. All included unselected atoms/H and inactive conformers remain exact.\n\n## Implemented milestones and decisions\n\n- C1: locked Linux AmberTools 24.8 native generation, GAFF 1.81/AM1-BCC, selected-only\n  reduced optimization, immutable report/model/proposal, bounded descendant lifecycle.\n- C2: complete ff14SB protein chains/components and optional neutral TIP3P context;\n  same/separate-entry ligand/residue selections, full boundary/exclusion/scaled1-4\n  terms, actual captured starts and dynamic native neighbors.\n- C3: typed capability/capture/proposal/Apply APIs, authoritative server capture,\n  SQLite-serialized dependency validation and atomic existing-history publication.\n- C4: native setup/progress/cancel/report/preview/Apply, Jobs reopening, responsive\n  app-owned session generations, accessible keyboard/touch/theme/zoom controls and\n  repaired preview handoff/jobs-WebSocket disconnect cleanup.\n- C5: science/prerequisite/failure/force-difference qualification, actual preceding\n  reader, disclosed prepared 1STP and18,208-atom worker/native-browser measurements.\n- C6: consistent final versions, compatibility/release evidence and full-diff review.\n\nApproved contract: `docs/plans/issue-82-selection-minimization.md`.\nAppend-only decisions D-108\u2013112 document model/active-conformer/context/publication,\nshortcut and qualification boundaries. Global product specification/plan are retained.\nCheckpoint history must be preserved with a normal merge commit.\n\n## Deliberate scope and scientific limitations\n\nOne bounded AMBER-family profile replaces speculative multiple profiles; complete\nchosen chains replace cropped/capped shells; active conformers replace batch pairing.\nNonconverged results may be inspected but cannot Apply. Visibility never chooses\nphysical inputs. Automatic repair/H/protonation and a universal calculation framework\nare excluded. Deferred covalent protein\u2013ligand adducts and new cross-entry topology\nare tracked in #86; no adduct implementation is claimed.\n\nComplete existing topology, explicit H, assigned organic charges, and ordinary identity\nare required. Unknown/unsupported inputs refuse the whole job. No force-field fallback,\nembedding or canonical chemistry repair. Unsupported ions/metals/PTMs/crosslinks/\ncofactors and unqualified native carboxylate encodings remain refused. The model is\nlocal relaxation, not a native/binding pose, solvation or protonation certificate.\nEnvironment uses nonperiodic12 \u00c5 cutoff / 10 \u00c5 LJ switch / RF 78.3; isolated uses NoCutoff.\nIndependent final maximum movable gradient must be \u2264 10 kJ/(mol nm).\n\nPrepared1STP preserves all 901 observed heavy rows, with disclosed offline modeled\ntermini/H/generated-only stereo correction; neutral CCD biotin does not qualify a\nphysiological/anionic microstate. Eight translated full chains measure capacity,\nnot a biological oligomer. Host measurements are not universal hardware guarantees.\n\n## Installation, migration and compatibility\n\nSeparately install `tools/ambertools-linux-64.lock` and configure\n`MOLWEAVE_AMBERTOOLS_PREFIX` for API/worker. No job installs/downloads anything;\nmissing tooling yields capability diagnostics while normal editing remains available.\nNative package/build/data/executable identities are checked and retained.\n\nNo database or structural-schema migration: Alembic 0014, project/viewer/archive 2,\nnormalized/selection 1. Original uploads/IDs/topology/metadata remain exact. Archived\njobs retain immutable proposal/report/model history, with fresh Apply disabled after\nID remapping; preview display/session state is transient. Actual tagged 0.19 reader\nretains generic data/history/jobs/archive re-export, without new authoring support.\nUpgrade client/API together; use complete managed-data backups and existing downgrade\nguards for rollback. No application dependency upgrade.\n\nStable minor 0.19.0 \u2192 0.20.0 reflects new public UI/API/scientific functionality while\nretaining compatibility. All five authoritative version sources match. After normal\nmerge, repeat the complete gate on exact master, then create annotated v0.20.0 and\npublish a stable release. Postpublication evidence will be integrated through a\nnormal docs PR; the runtime tag will remain fixed.\n\n## Verification and review\n\nAll **18 final-version release commands pass** on clean-start b0b061d53e6c2a6c680b9ca1891e00bcc23f3b51,\nwith unchanged runtime/test/tool source: **1,038 Python, 265 frontend, 8 supervisor,\n264 browser passes / 50 intentional layout skips**, zero failures/retries/native\nscientific skips. Frozen uv/pnpm installs, fresh Alembic 0014, Ruff, mypy (87 files), lint,\ntypes, frontend/supervisor tests, production build, full Playwright matrix, diff,\nall five versions, locked native verification and final 0.20 producer / actual\ntagged 0.19 reader pass. Only documentation/evidence follows the gate.\n\nRetained commands/environments/source hashes/timings and lossless logs are in\n`docs/assets/minimization/c6-candidate-gate.json`; fixture/toolchain/native-browser/\nperformance/compatibility evidence accompanies it. Diagnostics remain separately\nidentified. Existing Alembic deprecation and lazy Mol* bundle advisories remain.\n\nC5 qualifies 70 supported protein graphs / 26 native force-difference cases; worker\nligand/prepared 1STP/18,208-atom cases meet 120 s setup / 60 s optimization / 2 GiB aggregate\nRSS / 5 s actual-SQM cancellation. Native trusted-event preview/Discard 500 ms and\nlongest-task 750 ms plus unchanged existing movement performance assertions pass.\n\nFull-diff local implementer self-review is retained in `c6-review.md`; no independent\napproval is claimed. Request integration review and address any actionable findings;\nrequired checks/reviews/protections and unresolved conversations remain merge gates.\n\nThe complete browser gate caught a 320 px movement-toolbar obstruction from the\nnew sibling button. The shared row now wraps without shrinking touch targets; the\nunchanged failing case and complete repeated gate pass. Diagnostic logs/trace remain\nseparate from final passing evidence.\n\n[Candidate gate](https://github.com/ManuelSe/Neistra/blob/e3e6a786a192a32795265ba0db9496c905464656/docs/assets/minimization/c6-candidate-gate.json) \u00b7\n[Full-diff self-review](https://github.com/ManuelSe/Neistra/blob/e3e6a786a192a32795265ba0db9496c905464656/docs/assets/minimization/c6-review.md)\n",
